          %title Contents
          %p
            The European mathematician
            %strong Alexander Grothendieck
            (in French sometimes Alexandre Grothendieck), created a very influential body of work foundational for (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"}> algebraic
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            but also for modern
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            more generally. He is widely regarded as a singularly important figure of 20th century mathematics and his ideas continue to be highly influential in the 21st century.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Grothendieck"} Wikipedia article
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Colin+McLarty"}> Colin McLarty
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Life of Alexander Grothendieck &amp; Topos Theory
                %em Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal
                (June 2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/81sPQGIWEfM"}> YT
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Initially working on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            by developing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+and+topos+theory"} sheaf and topos theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            and formulating algebraic geometry in these terms (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+spaces"}> locally ringed spaces
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            further developed independently and today serves as the foundation also for other kinds of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theoretic
            refinement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            serves as the foundation for modern
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
