          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Grothendieck’s geometric work is documented in texts known as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EGA"} EGA
            (with
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieudonn%C3%A9"} Dieudonné
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA"} SGA
            of the seminars at l’IHÉS, Bures-sur-Yvette, where he was based at the time. (See the
            %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Grothendieck"} wikipedia article
            for some indication of the story from there until the early 1980s.)
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cohomology"} Čech cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A General Theory of Fibre Spaces With Structure Sheaf
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/Kansasnotes.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Grothendieck-FibreSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            In the late 1970s and early 1980s Grothendieck wrote several documents that have been of outstanding importance in the origins of the theory that underlies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em La Longue Marche à travers la Théorie de Galois
                (1600 manuscript pages written between January and June 1981, plus addenda etc. which double its length!) (see
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Long+March"} Long March
                for some discussion of the ideas.)
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Esquisse+d%27un+programme"} Esquisse d'un programme
                , (January 1984), in which Grothendieck sketches out a vaste programme of research, incorporating many of the ideas from
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Long+March"} Long March
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~leila/grothendieckcircle/EsquisseFr.pdf"} here
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Esquisse+d%27un+programme"} Grothendieck's Esquisse
            %li
              %p
                %em À la poursuite des Champs
                (also entitled ‘’
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pursuing+Stacks"}> Pursuing Stacks
                ’’).
                %br>/
                It starts with a short (12 page) letter to Quillen, dated 19 Feb. 1983, but then discusses a wide ranging vision of homotopy theory and its applicability to problems in algebraic and arithmetic geometry.
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Les+D%C3%A9rivateurs"} Les Dérivateurs
                (another 2000 page manuscript taking up some of the themes in Pursuing Stacks, section 69) Dating from the end of 1990 and the start of 1991.
          %p
            In the same time he also wrote voluminous intellectual memoirs
            = succeed "." do
              %em Récoltes et Semailles
          %p
            En Guise de Programme
            %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/Guise1.jpg"} p I
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/Guise2.jpg"} p II
          %p
            A chronological bibliography of Grothendieck’s published mathematical writings (
            %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/GrothBiblio.pdf"}> pdf
            ).
          %h2#texts_about_grothendieck Texts about Grothendieck
          %p
            For an account of his work, including some of the work published in the 1980s, see the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Grothendieck"} English Wikipedia entry
          %p
            The video of a talk by W. Scharlau on his life can be seen
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.dailymotion.com/video/x8juek_colloque-grothendieck-winfried-scha_tech"} here
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Reminiscences of Grothendieck, 2007 conversations of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sasha+Beilinson"} Sasha Beilinson
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luc+Illusie"} Luc Illusie
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Drinfel%27d"} Vladimir Drinfel'd
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spencer+Bloch"} Spencer Bloch
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands/reminiscences1.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Cartier"}> Pierre Cartier
                ,
                %em Alexander Grothendieck: A Country Known Only by Name
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/201504/rnoti-p373.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luca+Barbieri-Viale"}> Luca Barbieri-Viale
                ,
                %em Alexander Grothendieck: Enthusiasm and creativity
                (
                %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/Mathbiographies/barbierieng.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                %em Quelques idées maîtresses de l’œuvre de A Grothendieck
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~leila/grothendieckcircle/Mathbiographies/Deligne.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luc+Illusie"}> Luc Illusie
                ,
                %em Alexandre Grothendieck, le magicien des foncteurs
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cnrs.fr/insmi/IMG/pdf/Alexandre-Grothendieck.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  Une entrevue avec
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Giraud"} Jean Giraud
                (
                %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/giraud.pdf"}> pdf
                ).
          %p
            A recent article in French on Grothendieck is to be found
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://images.math.cnrs.fr/Alexandre-Grothendieck.html"} here
          %p There were two articles on Grothendieck’s life and work in the Notices AMS in 2004:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Allyn Jackson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Comme Appelé du Néant
